:["ibd2-acamol::treatment-role"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A patient receives ACAMOL — paracetamol (acetaminophen) and a combination cold product. Which information is needed before assessing the next dose?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Acetaminophen contributed by both products","explanation":"Total exposure depends on the shared active ingredient."},{"id":"B","text":"The combined volume of fluid swallowed","explanation":"Fluid volume does not establish acetaminophen exposure."},{"id":"C","text":"The combined number of active ingredients","explanation":"Ingredient count does not quantify the dose of the shared ingredient."},{"id":"D","text":"NSAID contributed by both products","explanation":"The question concerns overlapping acetaminophen exposure, not assuming both contain an NSAID."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Count acetaminophen from every product before assessing total exposure.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ibd2-acamol--standard--acetaminophen_total","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-acamol::acetaminophen_total"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"After excessive total exposure to ACAMOL — paracetamol (acetaminophen), which serious toxicity is the principal concern?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Adrenal suppression","explanation":"This is associated with other treatments, not the primary toxicity here."},{"id":"B","text":"Hepatotoxicity","explanation":"Excess acetaminophen can cause severe liver injury."},{"id":"C","text":"Ototoxicity","explanation":"This is not the characteristic principal overdose hazard."},{"id":"D","text":"Agranulocytosis","explanation":"This is not the principal acetaminophen overdose mechanism."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Suspected acetaminophen overdose needs assessment even before symptoms develop.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ibd2-acamol--standard--hepatic_overdose","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-acamol::hepatic_overdose"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which paired reassessment directly measures the intende