lain cardiopulmonary status."},{"id":"D","text":"The absence of pain in the ankle alone","explanation":"Painless edema can still have important systemic causes."}],"point":"Peripheral edema needs clinical interpretation rather than automatic attribution to volume overload.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-gabapentin--7-day--edema","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-gabapentin::edema"],"answerKey":"A"}],"questionCount":5}],"bankVersion":3,"sources":[{"id":"content-v35"},{"id":"label-ibd2-gabapentin","title":"GABAPENTIN CAPSULE [SCIEGEN PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.]","url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=16542ee6-0e0e-4d3c-8b32-60ff6ef48846"}],"sourceFields":{"drugclass":"Gabapentinoid anticonvulsant; neuropathic-pain agent.","mechanism":"Binds the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels, reducing release of excitatory neurotransmitters.","use":"Neuropathic pain/nerve-related pain and seizure indications. In an orthopaedic/trauma setting it may be used when pain has a neuropathic component, but confirm the patient's actual indication.","administration":"PO. Dose selection and interval depend strongly on renal function; do not use a memorized standard dose for every patient. Chronic therapy should not be stopped abruptly without a plan.","monitor":"• Watch somnolence, dizziness, ataxia and falls. • Review renal function. • Serious respiratory depression has been reported when gabapentin is combined with CNS depressants, especially opioids. • With tramadol or other opioids, monitor sedation and breathing more closely. • Peripheral edema can occur.","why":"Gabapentin reduces excitatory neurotransmitter release through the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels; it is useful for neuropathic rather than purely inflammatory pain.","availability":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex on 1 Oct 2026. Exact capsule/tablet strength was not recorded; verify the product and order."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Gabapentinoid anticonvulsant; neuropathic-pain agent.","id":"section-0-2c14eaada8e71b96"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Binds the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels, reducing release of excitatory neurotransmitters.","id":"section-1-cda945c25de391d8"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Neuropathic pain/nerve-related pain and seizure indications. In an orthopaedic/trauma setting it may be used when pain has a neuropathic component, but confirm the patient's actual indication.","id":"section-2-26ae2133cce22b3a"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"PO. Dose selection and interval depend strongly on renal function; do not use a memorized standard dose for every patient. Chronic therapy should not be stopped abruptly without a plan.","id":"section-3-1ef1e042b30fb08b"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Watch somnolence, dizziness, ataxia and falls. • Review renal function. • Serious respiratory depression has been reported when gabapentin is combined with CNS depressants, especially opioids. • With tramadol or other opioids, monitor sedation and breathing more closely. • Peripheral edema can occur.","id":"section-4-ec316d039684976b"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"Gabapentin reduces excitatory neurotransmitter release through the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels; it is useful for neuropathic rather than purely inflammatory pain.","id":"section-5-3f729c3fb9cc0af3"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex on 1 Oct 2026. Exact capsule/tablet strength was not recorded; verify the product and order.","id":"section-6-ceafaeb078d6024f"}]},{"itemId":"ibd2-avilac","title":"AVILAC — lactulose","itemType":"medication","capabilityRequirement":null,"exams":[{"id":"ibd2-avilac--standard","itemId":"ibd2-avilac","itemTy