 use of LEVOX — levofloxacin?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Suppression of ventricular ectopy by cardiac sodium-channel blockade","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"B","text":"Treatment of susceptible bacterial infection","explanation":"This is a clinical use of the medicine: Treatment of susceptible bacterial infections. Palestinian product information includes respiratory, urinary/kidney, and skin/soft-tissue infections; use should match the actual infection, culture data and local antimicrobial plan."},{"id":"C","text":"Prevention of valve-related thromboembolism","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"D","text":"Relief of bronchospasm by beta2 stimulation","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."}],"point":"Identify the main treatment role taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::treatment-role"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which product is most relevant to reduced oral absorption of LEVOX — levofloxacin through a mineral interaction?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An iron-containing supplement","explanation":"Multivalent cations can bind oral fluoroquinolones and reduce absorption."},{"id":"B","text":"An acetaminophen tablet","explanation":"It does not provide the mineral load described in this interaction."},{"id":"C","text":"A clopidogrel tablet","explanation":"It does not create the described mineral-chelation interaction."},{"id":"D","text":"An amlodipine tablet","explanation":"It is not the multivalent-mineral supplement being tested."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Multivalent cations can reduce oral fluoroquinolone absorption.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--oral_cations","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::oral_cations"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Which result best informs assessment of accumulation risk and pos