es."},{"id":"B","text":"Peripheral neuropathy","explanation":"New sensory symptoms can be a treatment-related warning."},{"id":"C","text":"Gastrointestinal bleeding","explanation":"This does not best explain the new distal sensory pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"Orthostatic hypotension","explanation":"This mainly produces symptoms associated with a postural pressure fall."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"New sensory symptoms during susceptible treatment need review.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--neuropathy","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::neuropathy"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which ECG change is relevant to the repolarization warning in LEVOX — levofloxacin therapy?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An isolated change in displayed gain","explanation":"Gain is a display setting rather than the cardiac repolarization interval."},{"id":"B","text":"An unchanged regular R-R interval","explanation":"Current regularity does not measure the QT interval."},{"id":"C","text":"A fixed normal PR interval","explanation":"This does not identify prolonged ventricular repolarization."},{"id":"D","text":"QT prolongation","explanation":"Prolonged ventricular repolarization can increase risk of torsades in a susceptible setting."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"QT-prolonging treatment requires attention to rhythm and electrolyte context.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--qt","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::qt"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"During LEVOX — levofloxacin therapy, which new bowel pattern most warrants assessment for antibiotic-associated colitis?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Hard stool with straining","explanation":"This points toward constipation rather than colitis-related diarrhea."},{"id":"B","text":"Frequent, persistent watery diarrhea","explanation":"Persistent diarrhea during antibiotic exposure needs assessment for C. difficile and other causes."},{"id":"C","text":"Reduced stool frequency during immobility","explanation":"This does not identify the complication being tested."},{"id":"D","text":"Normal formed stool after breakfast","explanation":"This is not a new concerning diarrhea pattern."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Significant antibiotic-associated diarrhea requires evaluation.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--antibiotic_diarrhea","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::antibiotic_diarrhea"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"A bacterial infection is being treated with LEVOX — levofloxacin. Which paired findings most directly inform whether the antimicrobial plan remains suitable?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Pain response and analgesic requirement","explanation":"These can improve without establishing antimicrobial susceptibility."},{"id":"B","text":"Appetite and bowel frequency","explanation":"These inform general tolerance but not the organism-directed treatment decision."},{"id":"C","text":"Fluid balance and serum sodium","explanation":"These inform hydration but do not establish antimicrobial appropriateness."},{"id":"D","text":"Infection response and culture susceptibility","explanation":"Clinical progress and organism susceptibility inform appropriateness."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Use clinical response, cultures, and the authorized antimicrobial plan.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--standard--antimicrobial_response","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-levox-levofloxacin::antimicrobial_response"],"answerKey":"D"}],"questionCount":10},{"id":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin--advanced","itemId":"ibd2-levox-levofloxacin","itemType":"medication","title":"LEVOX — levofloxacin","stage":"advanced","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":true,"secondsPerQuestion":90,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds m